example.code:
var info = LogComponents.GetCallerInfo();
Console.WriteLine(info);
// Output: AvatarOptionObject-ToReturn-57

var rawXml    = "<Settings><Mode>enabled</Mode></Settings>";
var formatted = LogComponents.FormatXml(rawXml);
Console.WriteLine(formatted);
// Output:
// ```xml
//     <Settings><Mode>enabled</Mode></Settings>
// ```

var myObject = new MyObject();
DuJson.ExportFile<MyObject>(myObject, @"C:\Path\to\file.json"); // formatted
DuJson.ExportFile<MyObject>(myObject, @"C:\Path\to\file.json", false); //unformatted

remarks.para:
        Defined here because it is built in StartApp(), but used in RunScript(), and I think this is
        easier to read/understand than something like:




twsSession = StartApp();
